\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs40 \i\f1\fs40 Concerning the Service}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 The death of a member of the Church should be reported as soon as\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 possible to, and arrangements for the funeral should be made in\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 consultation with, the Minister of the Congregation.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 Baptized Christians are properly buried from the church. The service\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 should be held at a time when the congregation has opportunity to be\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 present.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 The coffin is to be closed before the service, and it remains closed\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 thereafter. It is appropriate that it be covered with a pall or other\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 suitable covering.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 If necessary, or if desired, all or part of the service of Committal\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 may be said in the church. If preferred, the Committal service may take\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 place before the service in the church.  It may also be used prior to\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 cremation.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 A priest normally presides at the service.  It is appropriate that the\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 bishop, when present, preside at the Eucharist and pronounce the\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 Commendation.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 It is desirable that the Lesson from the Old Testament, and the\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 Epistle, be read by lay persons.}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 \par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 When the services of a priest cannot be obtained, a deacon or lay\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 reader may preside at the service.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 At the burial of a child, the passages from Lamentations, 1 John, and\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 John 6, together with Psalm 23, are recommended.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 It is customary that the celebrant meet the body and go before it into\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 the church or towards the grave.}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 \par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 The anthems at the beginning of the service are sung or said as the\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 body is borne into the church, or during the entrance of the ministers,\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f1\fs20 or by the celebrant standing in the accustomed place.}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}\column 
