{\plain \fs48 \f1\fs48 The Burial of the Dead:\par
}{\plain \fs48 \f1\fs48 Rite One}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 All stand while one or more of the following anthems are sung or said}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 I am the resurrection and the life, saith the Lord;\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 he that believeth in me, though he were dead, yet shall he live;\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 and whosoever liveth and believeth in me shall never die.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 I know that my Redeemer liveth,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 and that he shall stand at the latter day upon the earth;\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 and though this body be destroyed, yet shall I see God;\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 whom I shall see for myself and mine eyes shall behold,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 and not as a stranger.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 For none of us liveth to himself,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 and no man dieth to himself.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 For if we live, we live unto the Lord.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 and if we die, we die unto the Lord.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 Whether we live, therefore, or die, we are the Lord's.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 Blessed are the dead who die in the Lord;\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1 even so saith the Spirit, for they rest from their labors.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f1   \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f1\fs20 The Celebrant says one of the following Collects, first saying}{\plain \fs24 \f1 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
